}

steps.body:
`new int[rows][cols]` makes a rectangular grid where every cell starts at `0`. Fill it with nested loops when each value comes from its position:

```java
int[][] grid = new int[3][4]; // 3 rows, 4 columns
for (int r = 0; r < grid.length; r++) {
    for (int c = 0; c < grid[r].length; c++) {
        grid[r][c] = r * 10 + c;
    }
}
```

A row sum walks along one row, so rows go outside and columns inside. A column sum walks down one column, so flip the loops: columns outside, rows inside. Every row of a rectangular grid has the same length, so `grid[0].length` is the column count:

```java
for (int c = 0; c < grid[0].length; c++) {
    int sum = 0;
    for (int r = 0; r < grid.length; r++) {
        sum += grid[r][c];
    }
    System.out.println("Column " + c + " sum: " + sum);
}
```

The main diagonal runs from the top left to the bottom right, where the row equals the column. One loop reads it with `grid[i][i]`, and it only makes sense for a square grid.

Gotcha: declare `sum` inside the outer loop so it restarts at `0`. Declared above the loop, each total would include all the earlier ones.

example.code:
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int rows = 3;
        int cols = 3;
        int[][] grid = new int[rows][cols];
        for (int r = 0; r < rows; r++) {
            for (int c = 0; c < cols; c++) {
                grid[r][c] = r + c;
            }
        }

        for (int r = 0; r < rows; r++) {
            int sum = 0;
            for (int c = 0; c < cols; c++) {
                sum += grid[r][c];
            }
            System.out.println("Row " + r + " sum: " + sum);
        }

        for (int c = 0; c < cols; c++) {
            int sum = 0;
            for (int r = 0; r < rows; r++) {
                sum += grid[r][c];
            }
            System.out.println("Column " + c + " sum: " + sum);
        }

        int diagonal = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < rows; i++) {
            diagonal += grid[i][i];
        }
        System.out.println("Diagonal sum: " + diagonal);
    }
}

