steps.body:
A 2D array is really an array whose elements are references to row arrays. Each row is its own `int[]` object, so rows can have different lengths. That is a *jagged* array. Leave the column count empty and allocate each row yourself:

```java
int[][] tri = new int[3][];   // 3 rows, all null for now
tri[0] = new int[1];
tri[1] = new int[2];
tri[2] = new int[3];
```

Until you allocate a row it is `null`, so reading `tri[0][0]` first throws `NullPointerException`. Loop columns with `grid[r].length`, never `grid[0].length`, because each row has its own length.

Because each row is an `int[]`, the enhanced for loop hands you whole rows: `for (int[] row : grid)`. `Arrays.deepToString(grid)` prints nested contents like `[[1], [2, 4]]`. Plain `Arrays.toString(grid)` would print a type and hash for each row instead.

Copying needs care. `grid.clone()` makes a new outer array but copies only the row references, so both grids share the same rows and a change through one shows in the other. To copy for real, clone each row:

```java
int[][] copy = new int[grid.length][];
for (int r = 0; r < grid.length; r++) {
    copy[r] = grid[r].clone();
}
```

example.code:
import java.util.Arrays;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[][] tri = new int[4][];
        for (int r = 0; r < tri.length; r++) {
            tri[r] = new int[r + 1];
            for (int c = 0; c < tri[r].length; c++) {
                tri[r][c] = (r + 1) * (c + 1);
            }
        }
        System.out.println(Arrays.deepToString(tri));

        for (int[] row : tri) {
            int sum = 0;
            for (int x : row) {
                sum += x;
            }
            System.out.println("Length " + row.length + ", sum " + sum);
        }

        int[][] shallow = tri.clone();
        int[][] deep = new int[tri.length][];
        for (int r = 0; r < tri.length; r++) {
            deep[r] = tri[r].clone();
        }
        shallow[1][0] = 7;
        deep[2][1] = 0;
        System.out.println("Original: " + Arrays.deepToString(tri));
        System.out.println("Shallow: " + Arrays.deepToString(shallow));
        System.out.println("Deep: " + Arrays.deepToString(deep));
        System.out.println("Shallow shares rows: " + (shallow[1] == tri[1]));
        System.out.println("Deep shares rows: " + (deep[1] == tri[1]));
    }
}

